<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, Figure <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> and Figure <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> shows the training dynamics on HellaSwag, WinoGrande and MedQA respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Standard Deviation Results</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The std results of Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.4 Baselines ‣ 4 Experiment Setup ‣ GR-SAP: Generative Replay for Safety Alignment Preservation during Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 GR-SAP Outperforms Open-source Alternatives ‣ 5 Results ‣ GR-SAP: Generative Replay for Safety Alignment Preservation during Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.2 GR-SAP Outperforms Open-source Alternatives ‣ 5 Results ‣ GR-SAP: Generative Replay for Safety Alignment Preservation during Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> are in Table <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Standard Deviation Results ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiment Results ‣ GR-SAP: Generative Replay for Safety Alignment Preservation during Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, Table <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> and Table <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.SS2.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.SS2.tab1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A4.SS2.tab1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Standard deviations (std) for Harmful Scores (HS, %) and Downstream Task Accuracy (Acc, %) for the comparison of alignment data sources with a mixing ratio of $r=0.1$. Corresponding to Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.4 Baselines ‣ 4 Experiment Setup ‣ GR-SAP: Generative Replay for Safety Alignment Preservation during Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
